 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Brand Awareness Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"A brand awareness survey measures how many people in a market know a brand. It asks them to name brands in a category with no hints, then to pick the ones they recognize from a list, and often where they first heard of each one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Open with a screening question for category buyers, then the open recall question, then a shuffled set of brand names that includes your rivals and one made-up name. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> sets up that order from a description, with an answer table behind every round.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good survey questions to measure brand awareness?\", \"a\": \"Strong brand awareness survey questions run in a fixed order. Ask which brands come to mind in the category, then which listed names people have heard of, then where they first came across yours. How people rate a brand they already know is the job of a brand perception survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between aided and unaided questions in a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Unaided questions give no hints: people name brands from memory. Aided questions show names or logos and ask which ones they know. Recall from memory is the harder test and usually the smaller number. It has to come first, because names seen earlier leak into it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good length for a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Four questions carry the study: a screener, open recall, recognition from names shown, and where people first heard of you. Add another only when a decision rests on its answer. Region and age band can come from the screener instead of extra screens at the end.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a brand awareness survey template include?\", \"a\": \"A useful brand awareness survey template holds the screener, the open recall box, a shuffled set of names with one decoy, and the first-heard question, in that order. Describe your category and rivals to Emergent and it builds those screens with a database behind them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should you send a brand awareness survey to?\", \"a\": \"Send it to people who buy in your category, customers of yours or not. A sample of customers alone overstates awareness, since every one of them knows the brand. How happy current buyers are is a separate study, a customer satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can brand awareness surveys track the impact of a campaign?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when you survey before and after it, and in a market the campaign never reached. Brand awareness surveys that show the same rise in both places point to the season or the category. Only the gap between the two markets belongs to the campaign.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best time to send a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Send one round in the weeks before a campaign or market launch, and another soon after it ends. For steady tracking, quarterly fits most brands. Field each round in the same weeks of the quarter, because a holiday month can shift recall more than the marketing did.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track brand awareness survey results over time?\", \"a\": \"Hold the wording and the screener fixed, then compare each market with its own previous round. Subtract the decoy rate before reading any rise. In an Emergent-built app, every round lands in a database you own, with no cap on responses.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
